# W44-AUDIT-6 Phase 2C — extend M3 discriminator to W44-105 buttloop seed at e8/e9

**Date:** 2026-05-24
**Status:** [SHIPPED — gates a/b/c/d/e/f/g/h PASS]
**Parent commit:** post-`5942fc64` (Phase 2B SHIPPED)
**TSV:** `benchmarks/w44_audit_6_phase2c_w105_bisect_2026-05-24.tsv`
**Reproducer:** `cargo run -p jxl-encoder --release \
                  --features "parallel butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop __expert" \
                  --example w44_audit_6_phase2c_w105_bisect`
**Wall time:** 96.8 s (6 cells × 4 encodes/cell = 24 encodes + scoring)

## Source change

Single new branch inside `run_butteraugli_loop` in `butteraugli_loop.rs`
(line ~1524 `auto_gate_fires` predicate): when `butteraugli_iters > 0`
fires AND the resolved `high_colour_class_exclude` field is on AND
`w44_audit_6_is_high_colour_class(self.zenanalyze_proxies)` (M3>=80),
short-circuit `auto_gate_fires = false`. This mirrors the Phase 1
exclude at the symmetric site for the W44-105 buttloop seed scale
(default 4.0 at e8/e9 on screenshot-class content).

No new gate field added — reuses Phase 1's
`resolved.high_colour_class_exclude` (defaults `true` on Zenjxl/
Aggressive, `false` on Libjxl/LeanFaster). Env hook
`JXL_W44_AUDIT_6_DISABLE=1` is shared with the Phase 1 site.

`EXPECTED_DIVERGENCE_GATE_COUNT` UNCHANGED (still 28; no new gate).
`ALL_DIVERGENCE_ENTRIES` UNCHANGED.

